{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Your eyes have seen.</b> He testifies to this from what you saw happen in the matter of Baal Peor — for those who sinned in the worship of Baal Peor did not intend this at the outset; their initial intent was only to commit harlotry, as it says: וַיָּחֶל הָעָם לִזְנוֹת (Numbers 25:1). And even though the Torah forbade this because of the concern of idol worship, as He said: וְזָנוּ בְנֹתָיו וְהִזְנוּ אֶת בָּנֶיךָ (Exodus 34:16), each one of them thought that this would not happen to him at all. But the opposite occurred: every man who went after Baal Peor to cleave to his daughters — not a single one of them guarded himself by his wisdom from stumbling in the worship itself, until HaShem your Elohim destroyed him."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:23.302536091Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}